text: ['As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile a creature you control.\\nReturn target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Put a +2/+2 counter on that creature if the exiled creature was a Thrull.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a Goblin.\\nGoblin Grenade deals 5 damage to any target.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Elvish Farmer.\\nRemove three spore counters from Elvish Farmer: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.\\nSacrifice a Saproling: You gain 2 life.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Feral Thallid.\\nRemove three spore counters from Feral Thallid: Regenerate Feral Thallid.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Spore Flower.\\nRemove three spore counters from Spore Flower: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Thallid Devourer.\\nRemove three spore counters from Thallid Devourer: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.\\nSacrifice a Saproling: Thallid Devourer gets +1/+2 until end of turn.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Thallid.\\nRemove three spore counters from Thallid: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Thorn Thallid.\\nRemove three spore counters from Thorn Thallid: It deals 1 damage to any target.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Breeding Pit unless you pay {B}{B}.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, create a 0/1 black Thrull creature token.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Thelon's Chant unless you pay {G}.\\nWhenever a player puts a Swamp onto the battlefield, Thelon's Chant deals 3 damage to that player unless the player puts a -1/-1 counter on a creature they control.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Tourach's Chant unless you pay {B}.\\nWhenever a player puts a Forest onto the battlefield, Tourach's Chant deals 3 damage to that player unless they put a -1/-1 counter on a creature they control.", "Banding (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", 'Black spells you cast cost {B} more to cast.', "Blue creatures don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.\\nAt the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player may choose any number of tapped blue creatures they control and pay {U} for each creature chosen this way. If the player does, untap those creatures.", 'Bottomless Vault enters the battlefield tapped.\\nYou may choose not to untap Bottomless Vault during your untap step.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Bottomless Vault is tapped, put a storage counter on it.\\n{T}, Remove any number of storage counters from Bottomless Vault: Add {B} for each storage counter removed this way.', "Brassclaw Orcs can't block creatures with power 2 or greater.", 'Cast this spell only if no permanents named Tidal Influence are on the battlefield.\\nTidal Influence enters the battlefield with a tide counter on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a tide counter on Tidal Influence.\\nAs long as there is exactly one tide counter on Tidal Influence, all blue creatures get -2/-0.\\nAs long as there are exactly three tide counters on Tidal Influence, all blue creatures get +2/+0.\\nWhenever there are four or more tide counters on Tidal Influence, remove all tide counters from it.', 'Create four 1/1 white Citizen creature tokens.', "Creatures you control have menace. (They can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nTap an untapped Merfolk you control: Vodalian War Machine can attack this turn as though it didn't have defender.\\nTap an untapped Merfolk you control: Vodalian War Machine gets +2/+1 until end of turn.\\nWhen Vodalian War Machine dies, destroy all Merfolk tapped this turn to pay for its abilities.", 'Dwarven Catapult deals X damage divided evenly, rounded down, among all creatures target opponent controls.', 'Dwarven Hold enters the battlefield tapped.\\nYou may choose not to untap Dwarven Hold during your untap step.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Dwarven Hold is tapped, put a storage counter on it.\\n{T}, Remove any number of storage counters from Dwarven Hold: Add {R} for each storage counter removed this way.', 'Dwarven Ruins enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Dwarven Ruins: Add {R}{R}.', 'Ebon Stronghold enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Ebon Stronghold: Add {B}{B}.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.\\nSacrifice Thrull Retainer: Regenerate enchanted creature.', "Enchant creature\\nMerseine enters the battlefield with three net counters on it.\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step if Merseine has a net counter on it.\\nPay enchanted creature's mana cost: Remove a net counter from Merseine. Only the controller of the enchanted creature may activate this ability.", "Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature attacks and isn't blocked, its controller may have it deal damage equal to its power plus 2 to another target creature. If that player does, the attacking creature assigns no combat damage this turn.", "Enchant land you control\\nSacrifice a Thrull: Put three time counters on Tourach's Gate.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter from Tourach's Gate. If there are no time counters on Tourach's Gate, sacrifice it.\\nTap enchanted land: Attacking creatures you control get +2/-1 until end of turn. Activate only if enchanted land is untapped.", 'First strike, trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a -2/-2 counter on Ebon Praetor.\\nSacrifice a creature: Remove a -2/-2 counter from Ebon Praetor. If the sacrificed creature was a Thrull, put a +1/+0 counter on Ebon Praetor. Activate only during your upkeep and only once each turn.', "First strike; banding (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)\\nWhenever Icatian Skirmishers attacks, all creatures banded with it gain first strike until end of turn.", "First strike\\nVodalian Knights can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.\\nWhen you control no Islands, sacrifice Vodalian Knights.\\n{U}: Vodalian Knights gains flying until end of turn.", 'Havenwood Battleground enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Havenwood Battleground: Add {G}{G}.', 'Hollow Trees enters the battlefield tapped.\\nYou may choose not to untap Hollow Trees during your untap step.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Hollow Trees is tapped, put a storage counter on it.\\n{T}, Remove any number of storage counters from Hollow Trees: Add {G} for each storage counter removed this way.', 'Homarid enters the battlefield with a tide counter on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a tide counter on Homarid.\\nAs long as there is exactly one tide counter on Homarid, it gets -1/-1.\\nAs long as there are exactly three tide counters on Homarid, it gets +1/+1.\\nWhenever there are four or more tide counters on Homarid, remove all tide counters from it.', 'Icatian Javelineers enters the battlefield with a javelin counter on it.\\n{T}, Remove a javelin counter from Icatian Javelineers: It deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Icatian Moneychanger enters the battlefield with three credit counters on it.\\nWhen Icatian Moneychanger enters the battlefield, it deals 3 damage to you.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a credit counter on Icatian Moneychanger.\\nSacrifice Icatian Moneychanger: You gain 1 life for each credit counter on Icatian Moneychanger. Activate only during your upkeep.', 'Icatian Store enters the battlefield tapped.\\nYou may choose not to untap Icatian Store during your untap step.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Icatian Store is tapped, put a storage counter on it.\\n{T}, Remove any number of storage counters from Icatian Store: Add {W} for each storage counter removed this way.', "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\nAt the beginning of each combat, unless you pay {R}, whenever Goblin Flotilla blocks or becomes blocked by a creature this combat, that creature gains first strike until end of turn.", "Orcish Veteran can't block white creatures with power 2 or greater.\\n{R}: Orcish Veteran gains first strike until end of turn.", 'Protection from black\\n{W}: Order of Leitbur gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{W}{W}: Order of Leitbur gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Protection from white\\n{B}: Order of the Ebon Hand gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{B}{B}: Order of the Ebon Hand gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Raiding Party can't be the target of white spells or abilities from white sources.\\nSacrifice an Orc: Each player may tap any number of untapped white creatures they control. For each creature tapped this way, that player chooses up to two Plains. Then destroy all Plains that weren't chosen this way by any player.", 'Ruins of Trokair enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Ruins of Trokair: Add {W}{W}.', 'Sacrifice a Goblin: Regenerate target creature.', 'Sacrifice a white creature: For each attacking red creature, prevent all combat damage that would be dealt by that creature this turn unless its controller pays {2}{R}.', 'Sand Silos enters the battlefield tapped.\\nYou may choose not to untap Sand Silos during your untap step.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Sand Silos is tapped, put a storage counter on it.\\n{T}, Remove any number of storage counters from Sand Silos: Add {U} for each storage counter removed this way.', 'Svyelunite Temple enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Svyelunite Temple: Add {U}{U}.', "Tap all blocking creatures. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn. Each attacking creature and each blocking creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Target player discards two cards at random.', 'Thrull creatures get +1/+1.\\n{T}: Gain control of target Thrull for as long as you control Thrull Champion.', "Trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Deep Spawn unless you mill two cards.\\n{U}: Deep Spawn gains shroud until end of turn and doesn't untap during your next untap step. Tap Deep Spawn. (A creature with shroud can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", "Trample\\nOrgg can't attack if defending player controls an untapped creature with power 3 or greater.\\nOrgg can't block creatures with power 3 or greater.", 'Until end of turn, whenever a player taps an Island for mana, that player adds an additional {U}.', 'When you control no Islands, sacrifice Seasinger.\\nYou may choose not to untap Seasinger during your untap step.\\n{T}: Gain control of target creature whose controller controls an Island for as long as you control Seasinger and Seasinger remains tapped.', 'Whenever Dwarven Soldier blocks or becomes blocked by one or more Orcs, Dwarven Soldier gets +0/+2 until end of turn.', "Whenever Farrel's Zealot attacks and isn't blocked, you may have it deal 3 damage to target creature. If you do, Farrel's Zealot assigns no combat damage this turn.", "Whenever Mindstab Thrull attacks and isn't blocked, you may sacrifice it. If you do, defending player discards three cards.", "Whenever Necrite attacks and isn't blocked, you may sacrifice it. If you do, destroy target creature defending player controls. It can't be regenerated.", 'You may choose not to untap Spirit Shield during your untap step.\\n{2}, {T}: Target creature gets +0/+2 for as long as Spirit Shield remains tapped.', 'You may choose not to untap Zelyon Sword during your untap step.\\n{3}, {T}: Target creature gets +2/+0 for as long as Zelyon Sword remains tapped.', '{1}, Exile two creature cards from a single graveyard: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Aeolipile: It deals 2 damage to any target.', '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Balm of Restoration: Choose one —\\n• You gain 2 life.\\n• Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Conch Horn: Draw two cards, then put a card from your hand on top of your library.', '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Elven Lyre: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Implements of Sacrifice: Add two mana of any one color.', '{1}, {T}: Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.', '{1}: Add {B}. If this ability has been activated four or more times this turn, sacrifice Initiates of the Ebon Hand at the beginning of the next end step.', '{1}: Add {W}. If this ability has been activated four or more times this turn, sacrifice Farrelite Priest at the beginning of the next end step.', '{1}: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, target Orc creature gets +2/+0 until end of turn. If you lose the flip, it gets -0/-2 until end of turn.', "{1}: Icatian Infantry gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{1}: Icatian Infantry gains banding until end of turn. (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", "{1}{B}: Counter target black spell unless that spell's controller pays {B} or {3}.", "{1}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Forests you control become 2/3 creatures until end of turn. They're still lands.", "{1}{G}, {T}: Target creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", '{1}{G}: Target blocking creature gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', '{1}{R}: Target Dwarf creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "{1}{U}{U}, Sacrifice a blue creature: Create X 1/1 blue Camarid creature tokens, where X is the sacrificed creature's mana value.", '{1}{W}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{1}{W}: Target Soldier creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{1}{W}{W}: Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{2}, {T}, Discard a card at random: Regenerate target creature.', "{2}, {T}: This turn, when target creature you control attacks and isn't blocked, it assigns no combat damage this turn and you put a cube counter on Delif's Cube.\\n{2}, Remove a cube counter from Delif's Cube: Regenerate target creature.", '{2}{R}, Sacrifice two Goblins: Create three 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', '{5}, {T}: Discard a card at random, then draw two cards.', '{G}, {T}: Untap target attacking creature you control. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by it this turn.', '{G}{G}: Put a spore counter on target Fungus.', '{R}, {T}, Discard a card: Put a +0/+1 counter or a +1/+0 counter on target creature.', '{R}: Target creature you control with toughness 2 or less gains flying until end of turn. Flip a coin at the beginning of the next end step. If you lose the flip, sacrifice that creature.', '{T}, Sacrifice Armor Thrull: Put a +1/+2 counter on target creature.', '{T}, Sacrifice Basal Thrull: Add {B}{B}.', "{T}, Sacrifice Delif's Cone: This turn, when target creature you control attacks and isn't blocked, you may gain life equal to its power. If you do, it assigns no combat damage this turn.", '{T}, Sacrifice a green creature: Target land becomes a Forest. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', '{T}, Tap three untapped white creatures you control: Destroy target creature.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color. An opponent gains control of Rainbow Vale at the beginning of the next end step.', "{T}: Look at the top three cards of target player's library.", '{U}, {T}: Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.', "{U}: Homarid Warrior gains shroud until end of turn and doesn't untap during your next untap step. Tap Homarid Warrior. (A creature with shroud can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", "{U}: River Merfolk gains mountainwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", '{U}: Tap target green creature.', "{U}{U}, {T}: Target creature gains shroud until end of turn. Activate only during your upkeep. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", "{U}{U}: For each attacking creature without flying, its controller may pay {1}. If that player doesn't, creatures you control blocking that creature gain first strike until end of turn."]
flavor: ['"A whole skin is worth a thousand victories."\\n—Orcish Veteran of the Battle of Montford', '"Above all, a well crafted Thrull should be hideous—blasted of countenance and twisted of limb—to inspire fear and revulsion."\\n—Endrek Sahr, Master Breeder', '"According to accepted theory, the Grenade held some kind of flammable mixture and was carried to its target by a hapless Goblin."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"Although Icatia\'s Combat Medics borrowed much of their knowledge from other societies, their skills were their own."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. VI*', '"Although fragile, the Aeolipile could be quite destructive."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. I*', '"Although the Dwarves staunchly defended their walled city-states against the Orcs, their civilization was the first to fall, and its name was sadly lost."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. I*', '"As the climate cooled, many Elves turned to Thallid farming for food, while the Hunters honed their skills on what little game remained."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. III*', '"As the climate worsened, some Thelonites turned to fertilizing with fresh blood in an attempt to keep Havenwood alive and growing."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. III*', '"Because the Orc hordes attacked along the entire border, Scouts were essential to Icatia\'s defense."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. VI*', '"Born and bred of fungus, Thallids were nearly impossible to kill."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. I*', '"Brassclaws were typical Orcs—quick to laud their own prowess in battle, quick to jeer at their opponents, and quicker still to run away when things started to look slightly dangerous."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"Burn it down, you say? Now *there\'s* a stupid idea. What do you suppose will become of those overhanging branches, hmm? And then what do you suppose will become of us?"\\n—Ivra Jursdotter', '"By the time their enemies noticed the sea\'s changing mood, the Vodalians had often shifted formation and were ready to attack."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. V*', '"Come back, cowards! Everyone knows Merfolk can\'t wield magic!"\\n—Pashadar Dirf, Goblin Flotilla Commander, last words', '"Defending the outer trenches, we strained our eyes in the darkness. All we could hear was the Drums\' terrible pounding. Dobbs, on my right, broke first. Soon we were all heading for the walls."\\n—Corporal Peter Douglas, courtmartial testimony', '"Dwarven officers were tireless in battle, moving up and down the lines to rally their troops and boost morale."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"Dwelling in icy mountain streams near Goblin and Orcish foes, the River Merfolk were known for their stoicism."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. V*', '"Early Vodalians worshipped Svyelun, goddess of the Pearl Moon. Later she became a more abstract figure."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. V*', '"Elves often tipped their arrows with a drug that caused a deep but harmless sleep."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. III*', '"Even for Elves, they were stealthy little twerps. They\'d taken our measure before we\'d even seen them."\\n—Marshall Volnikov', '"Ever see a wall drop dead of fright, kid? It ain\'t pretty."\\n—Cpl. Dobbs', '"Except for a bare spot at the base of their skulls, Armor Thrulls bear interlocking plates and spikes with the strength of steel. Their design is almost artistic."\\n—Endrek Sahr, "Thrulls"', '"Goblins bred underground, their numbers hidden from the enemy until it was too late."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"I asked one of my aides how they do it, but all he\'d say was, \'Trust me, Mayor, you don\'t want to know.\'"\\n—Lydia Wynforth, Mayor of Trokair', '"I don\'t know which is worse, getting hit with those darts or having to watch them grow back."\\n—Orcish Soldier', '"I don\'t suppose we could teach them to *throw* the cursed things?"\\n—Ivra Jursdotter', '"In crafting intelligent Thrulls to assist in sacrifices, Sahr inadvertantly set the stage for the Thrull Rebellion."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. II*', '"Let it be known that Ailis Connaut acted with honor and bravery in the defense of the town of Montford, risking her life to scout the enemy\'s position . . . ."\\n—Proclamation granting knighthood', '"Let no one say we did not fight until the last . . . ."\\n—Headstone fragment from a mass grave found in the Crimson Peaks', '"Many Initiates sacrificed a hand to become full members of the Order."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. II*', '"May Svyelun and her tides favor you."\\n—Traditional Merfolk blessing', '"May you be strong and valiant, to defeat the enemies of the pure."\\n—"Leitbur\'s Prayer"', '"Never Surrender"\\n—Motto carved into a fragment of an Icatian wall', '"Not all armies enjoyed the services of a medic. For them, Balm of Restoration was that much more valuable."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. I*', '"Of course I\'m not a spy! The enemy has spies. I am a Scout."\\n—Ailis Connaut', '"Often greatly outnumbered in battle, Dwarves relied on catapults as one means of damaging a large army."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"Orcish armies often employed the smaller, swifter, and less intelligent Goblins as spies."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. I*', '"Orcs often greeted promotions to Icatian battle with anguished wails and pleas for mercy."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. VI*', '"Perhaps Goblins are good for something after all."\\n—Attributed to General Khurzog', '"Scholars still debate whether the Thallids were truly sentient."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. III*', '"Scouting is the art of balancing the need to go undiscovered with the need to get all the information you can. It\'s only by Leitbur\'s good grace that I\'m still alive today."\\n—Ailis Connaut, *Diary*', '"Stalwart Soldiers, you stand against the Homarids for Vodalia and for honor. Your homeland cries out for protection, and the moment has come. Now let your valor shine, and sound the cry to battle. Victory to Vodalia!"\\n—Marshall Volnikov', '"Strength it has, but at the cost of a continuous supply of energy. Such failure can bear only one result."\\n—From the execution order for Endrek Sahr, Master Breeder', '"Thallids are not ordinary enemies of flesh and bone and reason. They attack with no thought for our strength or of their own losses. I fear our Fortresses shall be overwhelmed."\\n—Kyliki of Havenwood', '"Thallids could absorb energy from the forest itself. Even Elves were at a disadvantage in fighting them."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. III*', '"The Brassclaws delighted in lightning raids on Icatian and Dwarven towns; an unprepared enemy is easier to defeat."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"The Goblins\' dreaded War Drums struck terror into the hearts of even their bravest foes."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"The Hand of Justice will come to cleanse the world if we are true."\\n—Oliver Farrel', '"The cooling climate forced the Elves to experiment with new food sources."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. I*', '"The cooling climate introduced a new threat to Vodalia: the Homarids. Once a minor nuisance, they thrived in the changing environment. Their ceaseless attacks strained Vodalia\'s defenses to their limit, eventually overwhelming the empire."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. V*', '"The danger in cultivating massive plants caught the elves by surprise."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. III*', '"The eerie, wailing Hymn caused insanity even in hardened warriors."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. II*', '"The few remaining pieces from this period suggest the Dwarves eventually made weapons and armor out of everything, even children\'s toys."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"The ground grew swampy; hooves and claws sank into the marshy earth. Snarls of rage and bleats of despair echoed through the trees as the waters grew higher and higher."\\n—Kyliki of Havenwood, "Havenwood Remembered"', '"The large brass claws worn by some Sarpadian Orc tribes were among the least feared weapons ever known."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"The magic at the heart of all living things can bear awe-inspiring fruit."\\n—Kolevi of Havenwood, Elder Druid', '"The powers of the corrupt will fade before the fury of the pure."\\n—Bethan Leitbur, "The Way"', '"The size of the obvious Fortress walls often misled foes. Actually, the Elves enchanted the forest itself to provide the first line of defense with tangling vines and stinging thorns."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. III*', '"The worst thing about being a mercenary for the Ebon Hand is having to wear a dead Thrull."\\n—Ivra Jursdotter', '"There are intriguing similarities between the Order and Icatia\'s Leitbur religion, suggesting the two had a common origin."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. VI*', '"There is no gain without sacrifice."\\n—Icatian proverb', '"There were often more Thallids after a battle than before."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. III*', '"They gave their lives to strengthen the Order\'s armies, until they declined this honor in favor of joining the Thrull Rebellion."\\n—Jherana Rure, Counter-Insurgency Commander', '"Those idiots should never have bred Thrulls for combat!"\\n—Jherana Rure', '"Time enough to become a Medic once you\'re hurt too badly to fight. For now, Icatia needs your strength more than your compassion."\\n—Lydia Wynforth, Mayor of Trokair', '"To create the first Thrulls, I only introduced alchemic elements into the Order\'s necromancy; Tourach\'s principles remained unchanged."\\n—Endrek Sahr, Master Breeder', '"Tourach\'s power was such that his followers deified him after his death."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. II*', '"Trained to battle the followers of Tourach, the Order of Leitbur was not as successful in later conflicts with Orcish and Goblin raiders."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. I*', '"Until the Rebellion, Thrulls served their masters faithfully—even at the cost of their own lives."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. II*', '"Valiant Icatia was the last of the Sarpadian empires to fall. Its faithful soldiers defended their cities to the very end."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. VI*', '"Vodalian Mages are remarkable. Their merchants bring them arcane lore and devices from across the seas."\\n—Lydia Wynforth, Mayor of Trokair', '"Vodalian Soldiers had some unique advantages. Often they would ride into battle on war machines rumored to have come from the far northern oceans."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. V*', '"We are no longer Nature\'s children, but her masters . . . ."\\n—Oath of the Ebon Hand', '"We\'d no sooner knock \'em back on their heels than that accursed sawbones would show up and patch \'em back together again."\\n—Ivra Jursdotter', '"When the very tides turn against you, it\'s time to consider retirement."\\n—General Khurzog', '"Where is it written that beasts must cause pain?"\\n—Delif, *Ponderings*', '"Without Combat Medics, Icatia would probably not have withstood the forces of chaos as long as it did."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. VI*', '"Without their massive numbers, the Goblins could never have launched such a successful offensive."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. VI*', '"Yeah, they\'re ugly, they desert in droves, and their personal habits are enough to make you sick. But I\'ll say this for Orcs: they make great spies."\\n—Ivra Jursdotter', '"You idiot! Never let the spies mingle with the Orcish regulars after completing a mission. Now we\'ll never get them to fight!"\\n—General Khurzog', '"You think you know everything there is to know about battle? You know Orc droppings! Underwater combat is three dimensional. Those thrice-damned Vodalians don\'t attack in ranks; they attack in schools."\\n—Ivra Jursdotter', 'A true follower of Tourach took pride in achievement to the exclusion of other concerns.', 'After the fall of Trokair, Farrel and his followers formally broke their ties with the rest of Icatia.', 'Although models of courage for Orcs, the Veterans quickly learned to fear the swift justice of their Icatian enemies.', 'Although my later designs were much more sophisticated, Basal Thrulls were no less a success."\\n—Endrek Sahr, "Thrulls"', 'Although the Elves of Havenwood lived in isolated villages, their swift communications allowed them to act as a single community.', "Although their methods were often brutal, Farrel's followers believed in the preservation of justice and virtue.", 'Although they had long been concerned about the Order of the Ebon Hand, the Icatians faced an even greater threat from Goblin and Orcish raiders.', 'At times, survival must outweigh all other considerations.', 'Dedicated to the principles of Tourach, members of the Order of the Ebon Hand demonstrated their devotion with grisly rituals.', 'Ebon leaders soon realized that non-human races often had special talents that could be exploited.', 'Even after the wall was breached in half a dozen places, the Phalanxes fought on, standing solidly against the onrushing raiders. Disciplined and dedicated, they held their ranks to the end, even in the face of tremendous losses.', 'Even one whose ears were closely tuned to the sounds of Havenwood could miss hearing a Scout move past.', "Even the most skilled of modern mages only partially understand the Conch Horn's awesome powers.", 'Exceptionally poor sailors, Goblins usually arrived at their destination retching and in no condition to fight.', 'Farrel and his followers became a formidable band of vigilantes, battling Icatians and followers of Tourach.', 'Farrel, a former priest, believed Icatia was far too complacent toward the Order of the Ebon Hand.', 'Fear the Knight leaping from the water into the air, weapon ready.', 'Followers of Tourach regarded all other religions equally: with open contempt. Not so the followers of Leitbur, who made it their mission to eradicate the Order of the Ebon Hand.', "Icatia's once peaceful towns faced increasing attacks from Orcs and Goblins as the climate cooled. By the time the empire fell, they were little more than armed camps.", "In the feudal days of Icatia, finding the Rainbow Vale was often the goal of Knights' quests.", 'Initially bred for sacrifice, the Thrulls eventually turned on their masters, the Order of the Ebon Hand, with gruesome results.\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. II*', "It's bigger than it thinks.", "Knowing the Hymn's power, the followers of Leitbur carefully guarded their pillaged transcriptions.", "Many Elven Fortresses weren't built by masons and carpenters, but created from the living forest itself.", "Members of the Order often played the Hymn on instruments made from their victims' bones.", 'Necrites killed Jherana Rure, ending the counter-insurgency.', 'No sheath shall hold what finds its home in flesh.', "Occasionally, an ally balked at wearing a dead Thrull as armor. The priests' whips, however, were usually enough to encourage a more practical outlook.", 'Orcs are not exactly known for their valor—although most Orcs have seen countless battles, only a handful have actually fought in them.', 'Relics of the Order of the Ebon Hand, the bowl and dagger bespeak the hideous cruelty of its rituals.', 'Scholars are uncertain whether it was the actual sound or some other magical property of the Elven Lyre that transformed its player.', 'Skirmishers engaged raiders before they could reach the towns. Although these units typically suffered huge losses, they never lacked volunteers.', 'Some said killing the Thallids only encouraged them.', 'The Chirurgeons patched up their fallen comrades with a gruesome mix of twisted limbs and mangled flesh.', 'The Elves gathered huge piles of rot to grow fungus. Out of imitation or forethought, the Thallids did the same.', 'The Elves never had a standing army; when battle came, they pressed Hunters, Scouts, and Farmers into a surprisingly effective militia.', 'The Icatian army easily repelled early surprise attacks by the Orcs on border towns like Montford.', 'The Thrulls bred at a terrifying pace. In the end, they overwhelmed the Order of the Ebon Hand.', 'The War Drums enabled Goblin and Orcish armies to crush the sparsely defended Dwarven cities.', 'There is a legend among present-day Dwarves that the Dwarves of Sarpadia will one day return to defend Dwarvenkind against a deadly peril.', "There's a chance to win every battle.", 'To become an officer, an Icatian Soldier had to pass a series of tests. These evaluated not only fighting and leadership skills, but also integrity, honor, and moral strength.', 'To the uninitiated, the Ring of Renewal is merely an oddity. For those fluent in the wielding of magic, however, it is a source of great knowledge.', 'Unsuccessful in their early battle for Montford, the Orcs quickly tempered their bloodlust with cowardice.', 'Vodalian Mages were invaluable in magical combat. Unfortunately, the Homarids raided with strength, numbers, and very little magic.', 'Was it the sight, smell, or aura of the Necrite that killed so effectively?', 'When creating a new War Drum, Goblin designers sought out the highest quality skulls. Serra Angel skulls were most highly prized, although most acknowledged that the skull of the exotic Sea Serpent made for a richer tone.']
